# These files are consumed by Linux (bash shebang / systemd unit parsing).
# They must never be checked out with CRLF: a CR in the shebang makes the
# kernel look for a program literally named "bash\r" and the unit fails.
#
# A suffix rule is not enough. relay/ops holds the scripts the deploy host
# installs and EXECS directly - `deploy-multiplex` and `multiplex-healthcheck`
# have no extension, so `*.sh` missed them, and on a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true `git archive` handed both to the release tarball with CRLF.
# The installer then wrote them to /usr/local/bin verbatim and every direct exec
# died with `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory` (exit 127) -
# including `deploy-multiplex --preflight` on the host that runs deploys.
# Pin the shipped directories wholesale so a new extensionless script is covered
# by default rather than by whoever remembers this comment.
relay/ops/* text eol=lf
scripts/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer text eol=lf
